| 17-0add-13deg-N2-1800s (run2) | 354.4 | 0.61 | top gap |
| 17-0add-12deg-N2-1800s (run1) | 267.5 | 0.60 | minor wrinkle |
| 15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s (run1) | 246.6 | 0.77 | clean ✓ |
| 15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s (run5) | 276.8 | 0.85 | top gap |
| 14p8-0add-17deg-N2-1425s (run2) | 217.0 | 0.82 | wrinkles |

The **15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s** condition (polymer_wt=15, bath_temp=9, pullcast_speed=6, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=250, nips_bath_wait_time=1600, mixing_temp=40, N2=true) is a strong Pareto candidate: run1 gave modulus ~247 bar + pore fraction 0.77 (clean membrane), run5 gave ~277 bar + 0.85 (top gap defect). Runs 2–4 showed wrinkles or gaps. Only run1 was clean; runs 2–5 had defects. This is a high-value candidate with large apparent gains but inconsistent quality and only one clean synthesis — **validation is required**.

### Validation Policy Check

- 5 runs of this condition exist; only run1 (clean) and run5 (top gap) are defect-free enough to trust mechanically.
- Run1 is the only clean, fully-seated specimen with both objectives measured.
- The apparent pore fraction of 0.77–0.85 would be the highest in the dataset alongside modulus ~247–277 bar — a large apparent gain.
- No independent clean repeat has confirmed this performance.
- **Validation repeat is required** before treating this as a confirmed Pareto improvement.

### Recommended Experiment

Repeat the 15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s condition exactly (mixing_temp=40, bath_temp=9, pullcast_speed=6, N2=true, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=250, nips_bath_wait_time=1600, polymer_wt=15.0, additive_wt=0).

**Expected objective benefit:** If confirmed, this condition would represent a strong Pareto improvement — pore fraction ~0.75–0.85 (highest observed) combined with modulus ~240–280 bar (well above the median). This would push the Pareto frontier substantially in both directions simultaneously.

**What this teaches:** Whether the high pore fraction + moderate-to-high modulus combination is reproducible. The prior runs showed high variability in both pore fraction (0.66–0.85) and membrane quality (wrinkles, gaps). A clean independent repeat will establish whether this is a genuine process optimum or an artifact of run-to-run variability.

