- **14p8-0add-17deg-N2-1425s run2**: (217.0, 0.82) — very high pore fraction but wrinkles present; run3 (287.9, 0.63) and run4 (259.7, 0.44) show high variability. Not reproducible.
- **14-0add-8deg-N2-1250s run1**: (103.6, 0.75) — validated with runs 2–4 showing (189.4, 0.71), (171.5, 0.63), (246.0, 0.57). High variability in both objectives.

### Validation Status

The **15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s** condition (polymer_wt=15.0, bath_temp=9, pullcast_speed=6, mixing_temp=40, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=250, nips_bath_wait_time=1600, N2=true) has 7 runs with:
- Modulus: 246.6, 240.3, 199.0, 221.3, 276.8, 201.9, 314.8 bar (mean ~243, high spread)
- Pore fraction: 0.77, 0.66, 0.68, 0.75, 0.85, 0.58, 0.51 (mean ~0.69, high spread)

The mean pore fraction (~0.69) and mean modulus (~243 bar) are both strong. However, the spread is large (pore fraction SD across runs ~0.11, modulus SD ~40 bar). The condition is genuinely promising on both objectives but shows high run-to-run variability. With 7 runs, the mean is reasonably established, but the high variability warrants understanding whether it's real process noise or something else.

**The 14p5-0add-10deg-N2-1500s** condition (polymer_wt=14.5, bath_temp=10, pullcast_speed=7, mixing_temp=45, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=200, nips_bath_wait_time=1500, N2=true) has 4 runs:
