Wait — actually, let me reconsider. The 14p5-0add-8deg condition (bath_temp=8, wait=300s) was run once with (189.6, 0.63) — decent but not exceptional. 

The most informative next step given the current data: **explore polymer_wt=15.0, bath_temp=8°C** (one step colder than the promising 15-0add-9deg condition) with the same other parameters. This tests whether colder bath further increases pore fraction while maintaining modulus. This is a genuinely new point.

