**Rationale:** The 15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s condition (mixing_temp=40, bath_temp=9, pullcast_speed=6, wait=250s, nips=1600s, polymer_wt=15.0, N2=true) has produced the highest mean pore fractions in the dataset (~0.69 mean across 7 runs, with individual runs reaching 0.77–0.85) alongside strong modulus (~243 bar mean). This experiment tests bath_temp=8°C instead of 9°C — a single-variable perturbation that could further increase pore fraction (colder bath slows phase separation, potentially yielding more open structure) while the modulus effect is uncertain but likely modest. The 15-0add-8deg-N2-1400s condition (mixing_temp=35, bath_temp=8, pullcast_speed=5, wait=120s) showed (252.6, 0.69) and (190.6, 0.64) — suggesting bath_temp=8 with polymer_wt=15 is feasible. This new point uses the optimized other parameters from the 15-0add-9deg condition, providing a direct comparison that will clarify the bath temperature effect on the Pareto frontier.

